# Never uploaded as site assets. This is the real control for the internal docs: on Pages
# they had to be redirected away because everything in the output directory was served,
# and a rule that only redirects still ships the file. Here they never leave the machine.
#
# NOTE: this does not make the repo private. It is public on GitHub either way, so the
# standing rule stands: no client confidences in tracked files. See CLAUDE.md.
# .git first: without it wrangler reads the whole repo history as site assets and
# fails on the pack file, which is larger than the 25 MiB per-asset limit.
.git/
# wrangler's local cache. wrangler-account.json carries the account id, and none of it
# belongs on a public site.
.wrangler/
.github/
.claude/
scripts/
worker/
node_modules/
source-files/
source-photos/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore
package.json
package-lock.json
